<title>USA: Nebraska Finance Authority yields 6.05 pct in 2029. [CORRECTED 15:10 GMT]</title>
<headline>Nebraska Finance Authority yields 6.05 pct in 2029. [CORRECTED 15:10 GMT]</headline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects to add that the deal is subject to alternative minimum tax.)</p>
<p>PRELIMINARY PRICING</p>
<p>NEBRASKA INVESTMENT FINANCE AUTHORITY</p>
<p>RE: $19,494,000*</p>
<p>Multifamily Housing Revenue Bonds</p>
<p>(The Arbors Apartments and Timbers Ridge Apartments Projects)</p>
<p>1997 Series A</p>
<p>SUBJECT TO ALTERNATIVE MINIMUM TAX</p>
<p>    MOODY'S: NAF		 S&amp;P: AAA</p>
<p>						Expected</p>
<p>    DATED: 04/01/1997	  FIRST COUPON: 12/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 12/01</p>
<p>ALL BONDS ARE PRICED AT PAR.</p>
<p> MATURITY		AMOUNT*    COUPON</p>
<p>12/01/2017		7,534M    5.95  %</p>
<p>12/01/2029	     11,960M    6.05  %</p>
<p>CALL FEATURES: 06/01/2007    102.00</p>
<p>		   DTP 06/01/2009</p>
<p>* - APPROXIMATE SUBJECT TO CHANGE</p>
<p>The compliance addendum MSRB Rule G-11 will apply.</p>
<p>The award is expected Friday, March 14, 1997.</p>
<p>Delivery is expected on April 3, 1997.</p>
<p>This issue is book entry.  DTC is pending.</p>
<p>Lehman Brothers</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
